(2716841, 375668, 11923, '<td valign="top">Certainly meets the challenge.  Focus on the person''s hair is very nice but I''m not sure that what is captured here displays enough to be associated with a roadtrip by the casual viewer.  The size is a bit small, but I do like how you can see through the window - which helps emphasize the subject.  I do wish there was more to see here though as it is, the image doesn''t hold my attention.  Greater contrasts might help bring the b&amp;w nature to a higher potential.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Certainly meets the challenge.  Focus on the person''s hair is very nice but I''m not sure that what is captured here displays enough to be associated with a roadtrip by the casual viewer.  The size is a bit small, but I do like how you can see through the window - which helps emphasize the subject.  I do wish there was more to see here though as it is, the image doesn''t hold my attention.  Greater contrasts might help bring the b&w nature to a higher potential.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 06:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716843, 376692, 11923, '<td valign="top">Technically the elements are mostly there.  Decent focus, could be a bit sharper, okay use of natural light - your whites aren''t blown out but the light is flat.  The composition is a bit iffy for me.  I think there are too many busy things here.  The boots seem to be the subject and I can see why the suitcase was added to give a bit more to the story but the design competes with the design on the shoes and the color looks brighter in comparison so its taking my attention away from your subject as named in the title.  Overall it doesn''t hold my interest.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Technically the elements are mostly there.  Decent focus, could be a bit sharper, okay use of natural light - your whites aren''t blown out but the light is flat.  The composition is a bit iffy for me.  I think there are too many busy things here.  The boots seem to be the subject and I can see why the suitcase was added to give a bit more to the story but the design competes with the design on the shoes and the color looks brighter in comparison so its taking my attention away from your subject as named in the title.  Overall it doesn''t hold my interest.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 06:38:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716854, 376518, 11923, '<td valign="top">I like the concept but the execution loses some impact in great part to the lighting.  The low light is giving the image a sort of dirty haze to my eye and might be affecting the focus (which seems a little soft).  Since the subject is the car in the mirror, the surrounding stuff in the background isn''t really adding to the image, imo.  I would suggest revisiting the shot and try putting a length of black velvet behind the mirror so you have a nice black background to contrast the mirrored image against.  Or simply crop the image to 1/2 inch above the top of the mirror and see if that changes the dynamic any.  I gave a 4</td>', 'I like the concept but the execution loses some impact in great part to the lighting.  The low light is giving the image a sort of dirty haze to my eye and might be affecting the focus (which seems a little soft).  Since the subject is the car in the mirror, the surrounding stuff in the background isn''t really adding to the image, imo.  I would suggest revisiting the shot and try putting a length of black velvet behind the mirror so you have a nice black background to contrast the mirrored image against.  Or simply crop the image to 1/2 inch above the top of the mirror and see if that changes the dynamic any.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 06:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716860, 373825, 11923, '<td valign="top">Cute kids and I can see the relationship to the challenge here.  I think the harsh light isn''t an asset to this image - the blownout whites are very distracting - and I''m not sure if it was a purposeful post processing move or a random result but the image seems overly contrasty.  You have some great colors but the contrasty thing is manifesting them in an unattractive way to me.  I like the action in this image, it feels very alive with all the people crowded into the shot but I do wish we could see at least one of the two children in the front, their faces that is.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Cute kids and I can see the relationship to the challenge here.  I think the harsh light isn''t an asset to this image - the blownout whites are very distracting - and I''m not sure if it was a purposeful post processing move or a random result but the image seems overly contrasty.  You have some great colors but the contrasty thing is manifesting them in an unattractive way to me.  I like the action in this image, it feels very alive with all the people crowded into the shot but I do wish we could see at least one of the two children in the front, their faces that is.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 06:54:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716865, 377092, 11923, '<td valign="top">Interesting capture.  I like what you tried to do, though I don''t know if you succeeded since I''m not sure what you were going for.  I like the abstract nature of the bright light trails and the colors are lovely.  In fact I could see an image that was simply made up of the yellow portion of the image as a print (or painting for that matter) on someone''s wall.  The section with the bike not so much.  I think it offers an interestingish place for my eye to explore but after a glance I lose interest - though sitting here looking at the image while I give my comment I am growing to like it better, bike included.  I think the lighting is good and the composition works.  Meets the challenge of course.  I am bumping this up from a 4 to a 5 as I''m still not in love with the bike portion, sorry!  Probably would be a six without the bike for me (I love abstracts).</td>', 'Interesting capture.  I like what you tried to do, though I don''t know if you succeeded since I''m not sure what you were going for.  I like the abstract nature of the bright light trails and the colors are lovely.  In fact I could see an image that was simply made up of the yellow portion of the image as a print (or painting for that matter) on someone''s wall.  The section with the bike not so much.  I think it offers an interestingish place for my eye to explore but after a glance I lose interest - though sitting here looking at the image while I give my comment I am growing to like it better, bike included.  I think the lighting is good and the composition works.  Meets the challenge of course.  I am bumping this up from a 4 to a 5 as I''m still not in love with the bike portion, sorry!  Probably would be a six without the bike for me (I love abstracts).', '2006-08-11 06:57:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716867, 374633, 11923, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge, though I wish more was done with the feet to convey their use in transporting people.  The lighting is okay though a bit bright.  Color looks nice, focus is good.  Unfortunately, there''s nothing more here for me as a viewer than 3 flipflop shod feet.  I''m not sure what would make the image more interesting to me.. perhaps a different composition, the feet stacked horizontally one on top of another.. maybe if this was in b&amp;w with some higher than normal contrasts.. I''m not sure.  Overall it just seems a bit boring and doesn''t draw me in, so I gave a 4</td>', 'Meets the challenge, though I wish more was done with the feet to convey their use in transporting people.  The lighting is okay though a bit bright.  Color looks nice, focus is good.  Unfortunately, there''s nothing more here for me as a viewer than 3 flipflop shod feet.  I''m not sure what would make the image more interesting to me.. perhaps a different composition, the feet stacked horizontally one on top of another.. maybe if this was in b&w with some higher than normal contrasts.. I''m not sure.  Overall it just seems a bit boring and doesn''t draw me in, so I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 06:59:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716869, 374642, 11923, '<td valign="top">Good use of the light, focus looks good too.  Not so crazy about the composition.  I am not seeing what you may have seen here, as its just a bit of a car that isn''t keeping my attention.  I don''t know if zooming in on just one aspect of the car would help or not.  By that I mean just the grill or just the headlight.  I do like the color and how it plays off of the chrome on the car but it just doesn''t spark much interest in me.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Good use of the light, focus looks good too.  Not so crazy about the composition.  I am not seeing what you may have seen here, as its just a bit of a car that isn''t keeping my attention.  I don''t know if zooming in on just one aspect of the car would help or not.  By that I mean just the grill or just the headlight.  I do like the color and how it plays off of the chrome on the car but it just doesn''t spark much interest in me.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 07:02:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716870, 373987, 11923, '<td valign="top">Nice capture of light trails but I''m not sure why that and the piggy back are being composed together.  The two could make fine subjects separately but here together I find they instead distract from one another - the trails pull the eye away from the piggy back, the piggy back do the same - and all to the detriment of the image.  The title indicates the subject is the piggy back ride, so to me that should be the subject.   Perhaps a change in position would have provided a better background or at least one less distracting.   The focus looks good and use of light (flash?) works here.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Nice capture of light trails but I''m not sure why that and the piggy back are being composed together.  The two could make fine subjects separately but here together I find they instead distract from one another - the trails pull the eye away from the piggy back, the piggy back do the same - and all to the detriment of the image.  The title indicates the subject is the piggy back ride, so to me that should be the subject.   Perhaps a change in position would have provided a better background or at least one less distracting.   The focus looks good and use of light (flash?) works here.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 07:04:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716874, 377605, 11923, '<td valign="top">I think this is a cute idea and you''ve got some great technical aspects to it.  Focus looks wonderful to me, use of natural light looks great too.  My biggest fuss is with the composition though.  With the title, I''m thinking the image needs a bit more of an ambience for the background - something that ties it even more firmly to a kid but also to a kid acting as though it were truly their ''wheels''.  Thus, I''m thinking a background with a jungle gym or sandbox would further the story by highlighting just where a kid might roll.  That said, the current background is far from horrible, it does work here but the overall effect for me is "oh a kids toy in a backyard" as nothing is here to energize my imagination.  I gave a 4</td>', 'I think this is a cute idea and you''ve got some great technical aspects to it.  Focus looks wonderful to me, use of natural light looks great too.  My biggest fuss is with the composition though.  With the title, I''m thinking the image needs a bit more of an ambience for the background - something that ties it even more firmly to a kid but also to a kid acting as though it were truly their ''wheels''.  Thus, I''m thinking a background with a jungle gym or sandbox would further the story by highlighting just where a kid might roll.  That said, the current background is far from horrible, it does work here but the overall effect for me is "oh a kids toy in a backyard" as nothing is here to energize my imagination.  I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 07:07:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716876, 377335, 11923, '<td valign="top">Great idea, definitely meets the challenge.  I like the long negative space but I don''t like the colors.  It feels very very drab and boring.. like a painting that hasn''t been cleaned in many years.  The focus is a bit soft but I find that it works for the most part.  The low light is both a blessing and a curse in my mind as its affecting the colors (adversely imo) and yet its giving a softness to the image that is appealing.  Still over all I found myself not too enamoured with the overlying effect so I gave a 4</td>', 'Great idea, definitely meets the challenge.  I like the long negative space but I don''t like the colors.  It feels very very drab and boring.. like a painting that hasn''t been cleaned in many years.  The focus is a bit soft but I find that it works for the most part.  The low light is both a blessing and a curse in my mind as its affecting the colors (adversely imo) and yet its giving a softness to the image that is appealing.  Still over all I found myself not too enamoured with the overlying effect so I gave a 4', '2006-08-11 07:09:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716914, 377221, 18073, '<td valign="top">I like this image a lot, beautiful scenery  and I like the contrasting colour of the chute.  Good job!</td>', 'I like this image a lot, beautiful scenery  and I like the contrasting colour of the chute.  Good job!', '2006-08-11 07:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716919, 375506, 18073, '<td valign="top">Not a bad shot, but for me its a little too static, personally I think a slow shutter speed and a little panning would have worked a treat here.</td>', 'Not a bad shot, but for me its a little too static, personally I think a slow shutter speed and a little panning would have worked a treat here.', '2006-08-11 07:42:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716923, 376444, 25787, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition.  I find the shadowey light distracting.  Maybe a little fill flash would have helped.</td>', 'I really like the composition.  I find the shadowey light distracting.  Maybe a little fill flash would have helped.', '2006-08-11 07:44:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2716982, 376628, 40430, '<td valign="top">awesome capture of blue angels, haven''t seen one like this before.  a little fuzzzy around the jets but at their speed directly overhead it is hard to get them in sharpest focus, or it might just be my 5yo monitor. either way this silhouette works really well.-9-   was this at the seattle show?</td>', 'awesome capture of blue angels, haven''t seen one like this before.  a little fuzzzy around the jets but at their speed directly overhead it is hard to get them in sharpest focus, or it might just be my 5yo monitor. either way this silhouette works really well.-9-   was this at the seattle show?', '2006-08-11 08:11:38.000000', NULL, 1),
