(2734486, 376718, 49326, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju maður!! Þetta er mega gott hjá þér. Núna er eina leiðin upp á við (nema þú sért að pæla að fara niður á við, treystu mér það er ekki gaman í fimmuklúbbnum). <br/> <br/>Meðaleinkunnin frá þeim sem skrifuðu athugasemd er 8.8. Og þú fékkst 21 athugasemd. Það er kreisí. Kíktu bara á hæstu myndirnar. Þær eru að fá 7.5-8.5. Mjög gott, mjög gott.</td>', 'Til hamingju maður!! Þetta er mega gott hjá þér. Núna er eina leiðin upp á við (nema þú sért að pæla að fara niður á við, treystu mér það er ekki gaman í fimmuklúbbnum).  Meðaleinkunnin frá þeim sem skrifuðu athugasemd er 8.8. Og þú fékkst 21 athugasemd. Það er kreisí. Kíktu bara á hæstu myndirnar. Þær eru að fá 7.5-8.5. Mjög gott, mjög gott.', '2006-08-16 16:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2734526, 376656, 43869, '<td valign="top">This is awsome!</td>', 'This is awsome!', '2006-08-16 16:28:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2734643, 376635, 52817, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and votes everyone!  This was about as close as I could get to the parked Air Force One so I framed it within the confines of the cemetary.  The "mystery" in my title was referring to the mystery of what''s inside Air Force One, not just the generic plane itself.  I do know that AF1 has about 4,000 square feet of "living space" but beyond that, it''s a mystery.  Of course the mystery was also referring to the unknown beyond the grave.  Maybe a better title would have been "Air Force One Beyond The Grave" ???</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and votes everyone!  This was about as close as I could get to the parked Air Force One so I framed it within the confines of the cemetary.  The "mystery" in my title was referring to the mystery of what''s inside Air Force One, not just the generic plane itself.  I do know that AF1 has about 4,000 square feet of "living space" but beyond that, it''s a mystery.  Of course the mystery was also referring to the unknown beyond the grave.  Maybe a better title would have been "Air Force One Beyond The Grave" ???', '2006-08-16 16:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2734732, 376656, 6520, '<td valign="top">Great win! Kudos on the ribbon!</td>', 'Great win! Kudos on the ribbon!', '2006-08-16 17:31:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2734748, 375880, 40718, '<td valign="top">Holy cow, it looks like you did get mauled by the "I think he cheated, but I''m too scared to ask for validation, I''ll just give it a 1" crowd.<br/> <br/>I''m not quite sure why you have an even bottom but an uneven top.  Was the prop frame not square?  Sometimes not being square to the facade will do that, but it should be both top and bottom unless you rotated to make the text horizontal and cropped the bottom. (ya, I think that''s what you did).<br/> <br/>The age-old advice to shoot at a different time of day may have helped a tiny bit as well.  We got the minorly distracting glare on the window and the lighting on the background looks a bit harsh.<br/> <br/>I think it was a nice, creative shot.  It''s hard to recover from 16 ones...</td>', 'Holy cow, it looks like you did get mauled by the "I think he cheated, but I''m too scared to ask for validation, I''ll just give it a 1" crowd. I''m not quite sure why you have an even bottom but an uneven top.  Was the prop frame not square?  Sometimes not being square to the facade will do that, but it should be both top and bottom unless you rotated to make the text horizontal and cropped the bottom. (ya, I think that''s what you did). The age-old advice to shoot at a different time of day may have helped a tiny bit as well.  We got the minorly distracting glare on the window and the lighting on the background looks a bit harsh. I think it was a nice, creative shot.  It''s hard to recover from 16 ones...', '2006-08-16 17:40:00.000000', NULL, 0),
