(2748633, 377116, 30049, '<td valign="top">When I first looked at this I thought I was seeing the back of a vehicle with a bike rack.  Then I noticed the bus, then that it''s the front of the bus.  Yikes!  So who''s getting the free ride; the bike or the bike rider?  Titles can be so confusing sometimes.  ;^)<br/> <br/>Overall, the quality of the image is fine, especially in the technical details.  The background, for me, seems distracting and a little flat or dull.  Small boost in color sat maybe?  Hmmm...<br/> <br/>Anyway.  Good to see everyone back into challenges again.  I had missed your re-entry.  Smile and keep having fun!  ;^)</td>', 'When I first looked at this I thought I was seeing the back of a vehicle with a bike rack.  Then I noticed the bus, then that it''s the front of the bus.  Yikes!  So who''s getting the free ride; the bike or the bike rider?  Titles can be so confusing sometimes.  ;^) Overall, the quality of the image is fine, especially in the technical details.  The background, for me, seems distracting and a little flat or dull.  Small boost in color sat maybe?  Hmmm... Anyway.  Good to see everyone back into challenges again.  I had missed your re-entry.  Smile and keep having fun!  ;^)', '2006-08-22 11:50:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2748831, 377602, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>Nice shot!. My eye went to the runner, over to the trees, down to the sky and then down the building skyline.<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>Nice framing with the trees. I really like the arch effect. Find the amount of dark trees distracting. I would consider cropping the three trees on the right. This would draw more attention to the runner.<br/> <br/>Subject:<br/>Meets challenge<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>Nice DOF and focus. I like the details and colour in the sky and clouds. Very effective lighting on the distant buildings. Green a little bit oversaturated in the trees to the right.<br/> <br/>Summary:<br/>Good eye to put this picture together. Not sure about your scoremay have been the imbalance between dark/light and your subject. Voters dont spend a lot of time looking at the picture, so 1st impression is important for their initial score.<br/> <br/>Good luck with future entries!<br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression:Nice shot!. My eye went to the runner, over to the trees, down to the sky and then down the building skyline. Composition:Nice framing with the trees. I really like the arch effect. Find the amount of dark trees distracting. I would consider cropping the three trees on the right. This would draw more attention to the runner. Subject:Meets challenge Technical:Nice DOF and focus. I like the details and colour in the sky and clouds. Very effective lighting on the distant buildings. Green a little bit oversaturated in the trees to the right. Summary:Good eye to put this picture together. Not sure about your scoremay have been the imbalance between dark/light and your subject. Voters dont spend a lot of time looking at the picture, so 1st impression is important for their initial score. Good luck with future entries!', '2006-08-22 13:14:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2748922, 377388, 62755, '<td valign="top">Gotta love the $4.88 Walmart flip flops. Mine finally gave out - under the fake suede is cardboard believe it or not... Nice comp.</td>', 'Gotta love the $4.88 Walmart flip flops. Mine finally gave out - under the fake suede is cardboard believe it or not... Nice comp.', '2006-08-22 13:49:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2749580, 376059, 48389, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely boat and you have captured some nice detail. Matches the challenge title well. The only thing I would say is because the background has a lot going on in it that maybe a shallower depth of field would have suited this better :o)</td>', 'This is a lovely boat and you have captured some nice detail. Matches the challenge title well. The only thing I would say is because the background has a lot going on in it that maybe a shallower depth of field would have suited this better :o)', '2006-08-22 18:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2749965, 377493, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Welcome to the world of Does Not Meet Challenge.  As you can tell by your score, your choice of subject was not well received.  Most of the voters were looking for things that moved.  In my case, I gave you a 6, as I thought your entry was rather well thought out and fit the challenge.  Interestingly enough, the words on the bike rack, the color of the purple wall and shadow were a strong enough focal points that I didnt even notice that the bike rack post had blown highlights down the center.  Overall, I think you found an interesting view of an everyday object but it just didnt say Transportation to the majority of voters.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club. Welcome to the world of Does Not Meet Challenge.  As you can tell by your score, your choice of subject was not well received.  Most of the voters were looking for things that moved.  In my case, I gave you a 6, as I thought your entry was rather well thought out and fit the challenge.  Interestingly enough, the words on the bike rack, the color of the purple wall and shadow were a strong enough focal points that I didnt even notice that the bike rack post had blown highlights down the center.  Overall, I think you found an interesting view of an everyday object but it just didnt say Transportation to the majority of voters. Tim', '2006-08-22 21:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2750511, 377445, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>First off let me say that I like this shot.  That said...<br/> <br/>What I like:  Overall composition is nice!  You have the model on a third line and the rope going down to the boat almost on a third line.  You have awesome colors going on.  Great exposure to stop the water and good DOF making for an image with depth even though there is no other objects to add to the depth.<br/> <br/>What I don''t like:  This really could go in both categories (like/don''t) but the lighting is a bit harsh on the subjects back.  It'' has great gold tones but you''re just a touch blown out in that one area.  I know that this isn''t practical in this situation, but a touch of fill light to bring out the details of his face would really rock here, but what can ya do...<br/> <br/>Why didn''t this score better?  I think I would have to agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=40106" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">shannylee13</a> when she says that it''s a touch to snap shot like.  What does that mean?  If you don''t have an emotional attachment to the subject, it just doesn''t ring a bell with the viewer.  I also think that it was a little bit of a stretch putting a kid playing with a toy boat in a Transportation challenge so you probably got a lot of DNMC votes.<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: First off let me say that I like this shot.  That said... What I like:  Overall composition is nice!  You have the model on a third line and the rope going down to the boat almost on a third line.  You have awesome colors going on.  Great exposure to stop the water and good DOF making for an image with depth even though there is no other objects to add to the depth. What I don''t like:  This really could go in both categories (like/don''t) but the lighting is a bit harsh on the subjects back.  It'' has great gold tones but you''re just a touch blown out in that one area.  I know that this isn''t practical in this situation, but a touch of fill light to bring out the details of his face would really rock here, but what can ya do... Why didn''t this score better?  I think I would have to agree with  shannylee13 when she says that it''s a touch to snap shot like.  What does that mean?  If you don''t have an emotional attachment to the subject, it just doesn''t ring a bell with the viewer.  I also think that it was a little bit of a stretch putting a kid playing with a toy boat in a Transportation challenge so you probably got a lot of DNMC votes. YoursTC', '2006-08-23 00:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2751448, 376656, 61790, '<td valign="top">Brilliant. Great light and colors. Great job. Congrats.</td>', 'Brilliant. Great light and colors. Great job. Congrats.', '2006-08-23 06:29:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2753964, 376033, 43340, '<td valign="top">This was all the photographer did: <b><i>I got some soft pads and attached them to my tripod legs. Took some ratchet straps and attached the tripod above and below the trunk. I used my remote and set a 15 second interval to take photos while I was driving.</i></b> <br/> <br/>WOW!!!  Now that is going the extra mile to get a great photo!  It''s going too far...maybe, but I love the creativity.  Awesome photo and a fantastic technique.  By the way, in what city does WalMart have a circular driveway attached to a multi-level parking lot??</td>', 'This was all the photographer did: I got some soft pads and attached them to my tripod legs. Took some ratchet straps and attached the tripod above and below the trunk. I used my remote and set a 15 second interval to take photos while I was driving.  WOW!!!  Now that is going the extra mile to get a great photo!  It''s going too far...maybe, but I love the creativity.  Awesome photo and a fantastic technique.  By the way, in what city does WalMart have a circular driveway attached to a multi-level parking lot??', '2006-08-23 18:50:14.000000', NULL, 0),
